<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung buys 54,000T S.America soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung buys 54,000T S.America soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Group has bought a combined shipment comprising 38,000 tonnes of soybeans and 16,000 tonnes of corn through private negotiation from South America, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>The shipment, bought from grain supplier Cargill, was slated for July 16 to August 5 delivery from a South America port, traders said.</p>
<p>Further details of the shipment were not available.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
